THIRD-PARTY COMPONENTS
================================================================================

BBSpecs is MIT licensed. It ships with the following third-party components,
each under its own licence. None of them change the licence of BBSpecs itself.

LibreHardwareMonitorLib
    Mozilla Public License 2.0
    https://github.com/LibreHardwareMonitor/LibreHardwareMonitor
    Reads hardware sensors on Windows. MPL-2.0 is file-level copyleft: it
    covers its own files only, and places no conditions on BBSpecs.

Photino.NET
    Apache License 2.0
    https://github.com/tryphotino/photino.NET
    The native window that hosts the interface on Windows and Linux.

Geist Pixel
    SIL Open Font License 1.1
    Copyright (c) 2023 Vercel, in collaboration with basement.studio
    https://github.com/vercel/geist-pixel-font
    The typeface. Bundled as a font file; the OFL places no conditions on
    software that merely displays text in it.
    Full text: src/BBSpecs/web/fonts/OFL-GeistPixel.txt

PawnIO (installer bundled on Windows only)
    GNU General Public License 2.0 or later, with a linking exception
    https://github.com/namazso/PawnIO
    https://github.com/namazso/PawnIO.Setup
    The kernel driver that reads processor temperature. BBSpecs ships the
    official installer unmodified and offers to run it; it is never installed
    without being asked.

    The copyright holders grant an exception permitting combination with
    independent modules that communicate with PawnIO solely through its device
    IO control interface. BBSpecs uses PawnIO only through that interface, via
    LibreHardwareMonitorLib, so BBSpecs is an independent work and is not a
    derivative of PawnIO. Its GPL terms do not extend to BBSpecs.

    Source, checksum and signature details:
    src/BBSpecs/Assets/PawnIO/PawnIO-NOTICE.txt
